  "id": "b1-02",
  "title": "Asuminen",
  "subtitle": "Housing",
  "level": "B1",
  "focus": "Monikon partitiivi ja genetiivi",
  "focus_note": "The plural partitive is used for indefinite plural amounts, after quantity words like paljon and vähän, in negative sentences and for plural partial objects. It is formed with the plural marker i/j + -a/-ä: tuoli → tuoleja, talo → taloja, huone → huoneita, uusi → uusia.\nThe plural genitive ('of the ...s') ends in -en, -den or -tten and often has two accepted forms: lapsi → lasten, asunto → asuntojen, naapuri → naapurien / naapureiden, asukas → asukkaiden / asukkaitten.\nExamples: Pihalla on puita. Lasten huone on pieni.",
